  "diagnosis_text": "The s3\u2013s1 link is down at both ends, and s3\u2019s rule for h5 still forwards to that disabled link. I\u2019ll check local connectivity at each host to distinguish this path failure from a host-access problem.**Fault localised to the s3\u2013s1 uplink: `s3-eth1` (port 1) \u2194 `s1-eth2` (port 2).** Both ports are reported disabled, and the link is absent from ONOS\u2019s active topology.\n\nEvidence:\n- **h1 \u2192 h5:** 3/3 pings lost.\n- **h1 \u2192 h2:** 3/3 successful, confirming h1\u2019s local connectivity on s3.\n- **h6 \u2192 h5:** 3/3 successful, confirming h5 is reachable locally on s5.\n- On **s3**, the installed flow for h5\u2019s MAC (`00:00:00:00:00:05`) still outputs to **disabled port 1**. ARP broadcasts from h1 also use that uplink.\n\n**Diagnosis:** The failed uplink blocks the installed forwarding path. Although alternate links through s2 or s4 remain active, s3\u2019s forwarding rules have not switched to them.\n\n**Next step:** Inspect why those two interfaces are down and check the forwarding application\u2019s failover handling. The evidence establishes the link-down condition and lack of rerouting, but not what caused the link to go down. I cannot repair it through these tools.",
